This allows us to embed code like the following in a traced module:
@torch.jit.script
def maybeTile(timestep, enc_outs):
  if timestep == 0:
    enc_outs = enc_outs.repeat(1, batch_size, 1)
  return enc_outs

Currently one can do it manually, but it would be nice to have it in core, since FFT functions have landed.
# for Nx2 tensors
def complex_multiplication(t1, t2):
  real1, imag1 = t1.t()
  real2, imag2 = t2.t()
  return torch.stack([real1 * real2 - imag1 * imag2, real1 * imag2 + imag1 * real2], dim = -1)
